# T27 — Phase 4 — Task intent classifier

**Phase:** 4
**Type:** backend
**Model class:** balanced
**Depends on:** R26
**Spec anchor:** [§Phase 4: Retrieval V1](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#phase-4-retrieval-v1), [§Retrieval Engine](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#7-retrieval-engine), [§Ranking Complexity](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#ranking-complexity)
**Standards:** Cadres coding standard (`/home/pete/cadres/shared/templates/coding.md`); Lattice project rules (`/home/pete/cadres/lattice/CLAUDE.md`, `AGENTS.md`).

## Goal

This task delivers the first stage of the Phase 4 retrieval pipeline: a deterministic, feature-based classifier that reads a user task statement and assigns it one or more intent labels (debug, refactor, explain, add-feature, test, docs, migration, performance, review, etc.). The classifier is the input to every later retrieval stage — anchor extraction biases toward intent-relevant token shapes, candidate retrieval weights source mix by intent, and the scorer applies a `task-type compatibility` signal that requires this label to exist. Per spec §Ranking Complexity, the classifier must stay feature-based and inspectable before any learned policy is layered on top, so that ranking remains explainable for the lifetime of Phase 4.

## Spec excerpts that drive this task

> "Pipeline: 1. Parse user task and classify intent." (spec §7. Retrieval Engine)

> "Ranking signals: task-type compatibility, graph proximity to anchors, exact identifier match, semantic similarity, verification status, freshness, scope, evidence strength, contradiction/supersession state, past usefulness, recent successful reuse, user preference compatibility, token cost." (spec §7. Retrieval Engine)

> "Phase 4: Retrieval V1 — Deliverables: task intent classifier; anchor extractor and resolver; hybrid candidate retrieval from graph, docs, memories, and events; scoring model with graph proximity, semantic similarity, freshness, scope, verification, and usefulness; compact response shaper; diagnostic response mode with ranking reasons; benchmark suite for realistic assistant tasks." (spec §Phase 4: Retrieval V1)

> "Risk: ranking becomes hard to reason about. Control: keep ranker feature-based and inspectable before any learned policy. Expose diagnostic scores." (spec §Ranking Complexity)

## Inputs

- Dependency outputs: R26 (Phase 3 memory-graph review verdict) — ensures retrieval can rely on typed memory streams, link tables, and verification status fields existing as designed.
- Existing files in the repo this task builds on:
  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/intelligence/` — current workflow tools that today perform implicit intent inference inline; T27 lifts that into a dedicated module.
  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/query/engine.rs` — current heuristic intent detection in the query path; behaviour to preserve and extend.
  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/lib.rs` — module registry that must expose the new `retrieval_v1` namespace.
- Standards files to honor: `/home/pete/cadres/shared/templates/coding.md` (file ≤800 lines, function ≤50 lines, nesting ≤3, single source of truth — no parallel intent inference helpers); `/home/pete/cadres/lattice/CLAUDE.md` (Markdown heading references in code comments where behaviour is doc-anchored).

## Steps

1. Read `docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md` §Retrieval Engine pipeline step 1, §Phase 4 deliverables, and §Ranking Complexity in full so the inspectability constraint is internalized verbatim.
2. Enumerate the intent labels the classifier must emit, drawn from spec language and current workflow tool coverage: `debug`, `refactor`, `explain`, `add_feature`, `modify_feature`, `add_test`, `update_docs`, `migration`, `performance`, `review`, `unknown`. Document each label with a short doc comment naming the workflow tools that depend on it.
3. Create `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/retrieval_v1/mod.rs` (new directory) that re-exports the classifier API and registers the module with `lib.rs`.
4. Implement `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/retrieval_v1/intent.rs`: a pure-function classifier `classify_intent(task_text: &str) -> IntentClassification` that returns a primary label, optional secondary labels, per-feature scores, and the literal features that fired (lemma matches, imperative-verb hits, error-keyword hits, file/symbol token shapes, question-form hits). Features must be a finite, documented list — no learned weights, no opaque model — so the result is fully inspectable per §Ranking Complexity.
5. Surface a `diagnostics()` view on `IntentClassification` that returns `(label, contributing_features, score)` tuples for use by the diagnostic mode of T30 and the working-memory inspector of T36; this is the contract that lets the ranker explain why a label was chosen.
6. Migrate the existing heuristic intent inference in `query/engine.rs` to call the new classifier instead of duplicating logic; remove the old inline heuristic in the same commit per "single source of truth" in `coding.md`.
7. Add `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/retrieval_v1/intent_tests.rs` covering: every label appears for at least one canonical task statement; ambiguous tasks return multiple labels with documented tie-break; empty/whitespace input returns `unknown` without panic; long input is truncated at a documented boundary without losing the leading verb; diagnostics output round-trips through serde.
8. Run `cd daemon && cargo build --release` and the verification test command; fix any clippy warnings in the new module before stopping.

## Files expected

- `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/retrieval_v1/intent.rs` — feature-based intent classifier with documented label set and diagnostics view.
- `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/retrieval_v1/intent_tests.rs` — in-tree tests for label coverage, ambiguity handling, edge inputs, diagnostics serialization.

(Implicitly required to make the module compile: `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/retrieval_v1/mod.rs` with module declarations, registered from `lib.rs`.)

## Verification

- `test -f daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/retrieval_v1/intent.rs` — confirms the classifier file exists at the expected path.
- `cd daemon && cargo test -p lattice-core --lib retrieval_v1::intent_tests` — runs the in-tree tests and asserts every documented label and edge case is covered.

## Coding-standard checks

- File length ≤800 lines per file (`wc -l daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/retrieval_v1/intent.rs daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/retrieval_v1/intent_tests.rs`).
- Function length ≤50 lines, nesting ≤3, cyclomatic ≤10. The classifier must use early returns and table-driven feature evaluation; no nested match pyramids.
- Schema parity: not applicable (no SQL in this task).
- No `TODO`, `FIXME`, `XXX`, commented-out code, or unjustified `#[allow(...)]`.
- Single source of truth: the legacy heuristic intent inference in `query/engine.rs` is removed in this commit; no parallel classifier remains.
- No broken windows: dead imports removed, every public name expresses intent.
- Doc citation: where the classifier comments explain a behaviour mandated by `## Ranking Complexity` in the plan doc, the comment cites that exact heading per `/home/pete/cadres/lattice/CLAUDE.md` "Markdown Heading References".

## Definition of done

- [ ] Every file in "Files expected" exists with real content (no stubs).
- [ ] Every verification command in tasks.json passes from repo root.
- [ ] Coding-standard checks satisfied.
- [ ] No deferred work: no item from spec §Phase 4 deliverable "task intent classifier" punted to a later phase.
- [ ] Legacy inline intent heuristic in `query/engine.rs` migrated to the new module in the same commit (single source of truth).
- [ ] Diagnostics view is exported and exercised by a test, ready to be consumed by T30 (scoring) and T36 (working-memory inspector).

